"There are no stupid questions, just stupid people", as Mr. Garrison from
Southpark once said...

But first, note that it's spelled "altar", not "alter". A place for
worship has nothing to do with change.

> * When exactly does your God gift you for #offers??  I have had
> characters that offered dozens of  fresh corpses and nothing other
> then 'a hopefull feeling' to show for it... :(

This message indicates that your "prayer timeout" hasn't expired yet. You
need to offer more before your God will even consider doing something good
for you or answering a prayer. You're still hoping for the timeout to
expire.

Once you get a message saying that you have a feeling of reconciliation,
you can expect nice things to start happening with more offerings, and you
can once again pray. Praying at an altar may also yield good things. After
you've prayed, though, you will once again start to see those "hopeful
feeling" messages, and you cannot pray a second time.

> * How can you uncurse an item without a spell/scroll?  Can alters do
> that?

No, altars can't do that. The usual way to uncurse a single item is to dip
it in holy water. A blessed scroll of remove curse will uncurse your
entire inventory.

> * Can you destroy an alter...and what would occur? (Avatar-induced
> death or just a ball and chain?)

You can't, IIRC. Using a pick-axe at it (direction >) yields the message
"The altar is too hard to break apart".

Strangely, the God "owning" the altar isn't offended by this, while just
pinting your finger at it with only the *intention* to write something
already incurs you his wrath...

